mcdt: turn the MCDT clock on instead of giving up when it is off

check_agcp_mcdt_clock() reads BIT_MCDT_EN out of the AGCP AHB status register and,
when the bit is clear, every MCDT register accessor returns early without touching
the hardware - mcdt_reg_read, mcdt_reg_raw_write and mcdt_reg_update alike. Nothing
in the audio driver set ever sets that bit; they only read it. On this board it is
clear, so MCDT is configured into a void: setup appears to succeed, the pr_info in
mcdt_dac_dma_enable still prints its channel number, and the only hint is an
"agcp mcdt clocl not available" line that shows up during teardown, where it is
easy to mistake for an artifact of the power domain going down.

Whoever enables it on Android is not in this source. Since the driver already holds
the regmap and already knows the bit, have it enable the block it is about to
program rather than silently skip it. The write only happens when the bit is clear,
and the result is read back, so a controller that genuinely cannot be enabled still
reports false and nothing changes for boards where something else did it first.

The register lives inside the AGDSP power domain, so this is only reachable with
that domain up - which is the case whenever MCDT is being programmed for a stream,
because the ASoC path enables it before touching the DAI.

--- a/sprd_audio/mcdt/mcdt_r2p0/mcdt_hw_r2p0.c
+++ b/sprd_audio/mcdt/mcdt_r2p0/mcdt_hw_r2p0.c
@@ -52,12 +52,31 @@
 	u32 val;
 	int ret;
 
-	if (agcp_ahb_gpr) {
-		ret = regmap_read(agcp_ahb_gpr, REG_AGCP_AHB_MODULE_EB0_STS,
-				  &val);
-		if (!ret)
-			return (val & BIT_MCDT_EN) ? true : false;
+	if (!agcp_ahb_gpr)
+		return true;
+
+	ret = regmap_read(agcp_ahb_gpr, REG_AGCP_AHB_MODULE_EB0_STS, &val);
+	if (ret)
+		return true;
+	if (val & BIT_MCDT_EN)
+		return true;
+
+	/* Nothing else in this driver set writes this bit, and on some boards
+	 * nothing writes it at all - which leaves every MCDT access below a
+	 * silent no-op. Enable the block instead of skipping the work.
+	 */
+	ret = regmap_update_bits(agcp_ahb_gpr, REG_AGCP_AHB_MODULE_EB0_STS,
+				 BIT_MCDT_EN, BIT_MCDT_EN);
+	if (ret)
+		return false;
+	ret = regmap_read(agcp_ahb_gpr, REG_AGCP_AHB_MODULE_EB0_STS, &val);
+	if (ret || !(val & BIT_MCDT_EN)) {
+		pr_err("%s: agcp mcdt clock would not enable (eb0=%#x)\n",
+		       __func__, val);
+		return false;
 	}
+	pr_info("%s: enabled the agcp mcdt clock (eb0=%#x)\n", __func__, val);
+
 	return true;
 }
 
